  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IOM: F&#xf6;rebyggande av k&#xf6;nsbaserat v&#xe5;ld, fas 2</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM: Prevention of gender-based violence 2nd phase - Continuation Prevention of Gender Based Violence NS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the intervention is  to contribute to the implementation of the Peace Accord and to the political, social and economic empowerment of former female combatants from FARC in their reincorporation process to civil life.

Two specific areas are proposed: 1) Prevention of gender based violence and 2) Promotion of women, political, social and economic autonomy. It is expected that at the end of the project the following results will be achieved:

1) A strategy for the prevention of gender-based violence implemented in eight regions with the participation of 300 women and men (former combatants and members of the communities) impacting 100 public servants.

2) Eight economic empowerment initiatives implemented with a gender perspective, with an impact in the communities.

3) Three Care Centers designed and functioning benefitting 90 children. 50 women and men participate in the elaboration of action plans and capacity building processes for these Care Centers.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IOM i Colombia har inkommit med ett f&#xf6;rslag till den Svenska Ambassaden i Bogota om st&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r implementeringen av projektet &#x201d;Prevention of gender-based violence &#x2013; second phase&#x201d;, med 14 440 000 SEK under en tre&#xe5;rsperiod. 

Det huvudsakliga m&#xe5;let med insatsen &#xe4;r att bidra till implementeringen av fredsavtalet och till f&#xf6;re detta kvinnliga Farc-kombattanters &#xf6;kade politiska, sociala och ekonomiska egenmakt i sin &#xe5;terintegreringsprocess till civila livet. Insatsen inkluderar tv&#xe5; specifika omr&#xe5;den: 1) f&#xf6;rebyggande av k&#xf6;nsbaserat v&#xe5;ld, och 2) fr&#xe4;mjande av kvinnors politiska, sociala och ekonomiska autonomi. Detta skall uppn&#xe5;s genom f&#xf6;ljande resultat: 
1)En strategi f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;rebyggandet av k&#xf6;nsbaserat v&#xe5;ld implementerat i &#xe5;tta regioner med deltagandet av 300 kvinnor och men (f&#xf6;re detta kombattanter och medlemmar av samh&#xe4;llena) och 100 tj&#xe4;nstem&#xe4;n. 
2)&#xc5;tta initiativ f&#xf6;r ekonomisk egenmakt implementerat med ett j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsperspektiv.
3)Tre f&#xf6;rskolor designade och fungerande som gynnar 90 barn, med deltagandet av 50 kvinnor och m&#xe4;n i utvecklandet av handlingsplaner och kapacitetsutvecklande processer i dessa f&#xf6;rskolor.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this project support is to contribute to the implementation of the Peace Accord and to the political, social, and economic empowerment of former female combatants from FARC in their reincorporation process to civil life. The intervention includes two specific areas: The prevention of gender-based violence and the promotion of women&apos;s political, social, and economic autonomy. This is to be achieved through a strategy for the prevention of gender-based violence; nine economic empowerment initiatives; and three care-centres. This project is the second phase, building upon the previous contribution with ID-number: 11004.</narrative>
  </description>
